# BEM Naming Convention for CSS

Follow Block–Element–Modifier (BEM) naming when introducing CSS class names.

- **Block**: Standalone component in kebab-case (e.g., `hero-section`, `user-profile`).
- **Element**: Part of a block, joined with `__` (e.g., `hero-section__headline`, `user-profile__avatar`).
- **Modifier**: Variation of a block or element, joined with `--` (e.g., `hero-section--large`, `hero-section__button--disabled`).

Avoid camelCase, snake_case, or mixing separators. Each segment (block, element, modifier) must stay in kebab-case.
